"1792777169032656709-abc52074-7d16-41fb-9adb-bf52e2967e2a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8fb79688ae9f98a37204201c6a95181cb5ae76dbc4f78f65310121b0a0896c68","event_uuid":"1781f413-8667-4b7b-9527-1655df381c92","position":{"commit_sha":"84260de72cf8dd8a378041e86d145b06d2db89e8","position":"1792777183961212882-1781f413-8667-4b7b-9527-1655df381c92"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0b5c4387c777405d9fad9f9e680e89c11fee02881820def1e6e5e41fa5670187","event_uuid":"58cb4559-1a9a-40de-b76f-69abc434101b","position":{"commit_sha":"46ee4d5f836bdcb093af7a3077640afa501d8cd4","position":"1792777233971831376-58cb4559-1a9a-40de-b76f-69abc434101b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"User-authorized comment-remediation epic exception on 2026-10-23: comment-only work does not need planning review; ordinary claim failed solely because its review pins 11 drifted workflow files.\".","timestamp":1792772707489664246},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Group23 grouped remediation is in progress from origin/main@cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a. Current scoped candidate edits 86 standalone comment regions across all 18 workflow files. Local audit records 11,187→2,943 words with 86/86 strict reductions, unchanged YAML payload and exact protected directives. actionlint and diff checks pass. The final focused workflow selection is running. Historical d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84 remains provenance; current-base cbc02f0e supplies exact before citations. Independent review, full make verify, Gerrit votes, and merge remain pending.","timestamp":1792776440766609892},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Signed Group23 candidate 31ed99d034f982593fa2ca3ef970d4d927345305 (Change-Id Ia0c431e8080b7242383d4cc491407add89d3ee1e) changes 86 workflow comment regions across the 18 scoped files. Exact current-base before and signed-HEAD after citations are in the external author draft. Local structural audit: 86/86 shorter, 11,187→2,943 words, YAML payload/directives unchanged. actionlint, make lint, 354 workflow tests (1 skip), commit hooks, and every non-full registered DD pass. The current base has 21 mechanism markers, all preserved; the ticket scope and DD count were corrected from stale 5. Non-author review, full make verify, Gerrit votes, and merge are pending.","timestamp":1792777233971831376}],"created_at":1788570418293746172,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"fd8de228-4985-4cd4-8de1-c037371a6115","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2499-92ca-330a-40b8"},{"link_uuid":"fa4482bd-defd-468e-b1fd-a808b1c07926","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"04ba-844f-8195-4f16"},{"link_uuid":"b812bf19-1957-48e0-90d8-980fba4b1dc2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"244b-4163-df5d-4990"},{"link_uuid":"87c04216-1a21-4d44-886a-07147b139168","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"83d8-a708-c69e-41be"},{"link_uuid":"3f846d3f-e010-4ec2-88fa-96903b79f1d9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"920e-79d9-6a5e-4de5"},{"link_uuid":"28a2fec5-7dac-4ec5-b4b1-21e6f8e187f2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3794-3a84-3a44-41f7"},{"link_uuid":"fd9e2419-a5fd-481d-aac2-acdbd373b392","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5394-5578-ee7c-493b"},{"link_uuid":"453e4ce8-2973-45f2-bfd4-6a8ea3aef6c6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"37ea-35ab-fd93-4d5b"},{"link_uuid":"48535317-6840-4725-9b70-22f3b99d0040","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c9b8-38b2-0ec0-4c15"},{"link_uuid":"621ca204-142c-40c6-ba64-5bac9d56c071","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"64fb-a7c7-bda7-4e2a"},{"link_uuid":"d3559e65-2886-46c3-b91c-eea2e9c22863","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8606-6030-1b41-4d9a"},{"link_uuid":"1f4ff75c-b277-4212-b247-c65192226ca5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d85f-5f5a-ee80-4bbc"},{"link_uuid":"7f5fbdb5-e1f6-4eb8-b812-bf7d63f3c298","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"506a-cb6d-23d5-4d3f"},{"link_uuid":"d9131f4e-69cc-45d5-bd53-ce27f5d73450","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7b97-0033-3ea5-4aef"},{"link_uuid":"3e743d6c-d11d-4cc0-a0cd-b3ae0dd2b079","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ffe5-87ef-0351-495b"},{"link_uuid":"b658fc90-b6aa-42cf-bff7-6adddb097f27","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b2b9-c03f-79d0-473d"},{"link_uuid":"c1ff4f6d-3b9e-41b7-bce4-691d9532c0ca","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e4e6-8d0a-4c37-4e25"},{"link_uuid":"3582516b-4bfa-40cc-892b-89ee6b7a851e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0a2f-a198-877a-432d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen reusable and operational workflow files contain explanatory comments that mix current contracts with repetition, narration, or history. Historical scope was audited at `d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84`. The 18 live workflow files and Terraform-config-inspect canary were revalidated at `origin/main@cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a`. Before-citations use this current base because workflow contracts changed after the historical audit.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only allowlisted standalone explanatory comments and adjacent blank lines. Keep current non-obvious rationale, security boundaries, failure semantics, portability constraints, and operator-visible contracts. Preserve all workflow data, embedded shell, expressions, permissions, triggers, action pins, assertions, user-facing output, and directives byte-for-byte.\n\nPreserve these behavior-bearing directive lines exactly:\n- `_artifact-probe.yml`: both `shellcheck disable=SC1091` lines.\n- `_mutation.yml` and `gerrit-verify.yaml`: all four `predates-gate-ok` markers.\n- `gerrit-verify.yaml`, `prompt-eval.yml`, and `_optionality.yml`: all 21 current `mechanism-ok: ci_gate` markers (9 in `_optionality.yml`, 11 in `gerrit-verify.yaml`, 1 in `prompt-eval.yml`), including the three Terraform-canary markers.\n\n## Scope\n- `_artifact-probe.yml` — Preserve secret-free exact-patchset checkout, sdist-first build, baked-commit/metadata checks, installed archive probes, schema/import walk, and shellcheck directives.\n- `_build-and-test.yml` — Preserve secret-free exact checkout; online-token versus portable local lint; pre-commit skips; old-patchset guards; ownership-routed dependency advisories; enforced sandbox proof; Linux/macOS, coverage, extras, and Node lanes; browser opt-out record; patchset timeout; integration isolation; Gerrit report coverage; trusted-main docs restore; and generated/parity/security gates.\n- `_eval-discipline.yml` — Preserve both callers, secret/model-free exact-patchset evaluation, named offline subset, and 300-second thread bound.\n- `_mutation.yml` — Preserve changed/all shard selection, empty-selection skip, 30-minute shards, always-uploaded evidence, hosted-Ubuntu namespace waiver, and exact predates marker.\n- `_optionality.yml` — Preserve fork-safe checkout; clean no-extra wheel and heavy-dependency absence; old-patchset guards; no-agents degradation; isolated per-extra environments, union resolution, absolute interpreters, and aggregated failure. Also condense the shell-comment block before the Terraform canary's if-present guard while preserving the main-definition/patchset-tree mismatch rationale, early skip before installs, all canary workflow data, the pinned upstream binary, opt-in environment, and three exact mechanism markers.\n- `codeql.yml` — Preserve schedule/manual-only triggering, six-hour staggering, cancellation, Python/JavaScript matrix, path config, read-only permissions with job-local security-event write, and intentional major action tags.\n- `compact-sweep.yml` — Preserve out-of-band single flight; full-history ticket merge; harmless 60-minute bound; sweep-only write; optional signing; dry-run/limit inputs; exit-2 warning versus exit-1 failure; no-pipe capture; always-written summary; and operation-linked no-CI fallback. It publishes no metrics.\n- `dependency-advisory-canary.yml` — Preserve daily/manual dry-run, single flight, writable full-history store, optional signing, deduplicated lifecycle/comment cap, release-only blocking, merge-not-rebase retry flush, and visible red result. The audit step remains `continue-on-error`; the alert step must fail closed.\n- `external-integration.yml` — Preserve manual/weekly billable boundary; provider isolation and loud missing/all-skip failure; committed overlays; Bedrock-only OIDC and regions; complementary partitions, per-test timeouts, usage evidence; Langfuse/Jira teardown; scoped S3 and Jira Cloud cleanup; and Linux/macOS Pandoc replay.\n- `gerrit-verify.yaml` — Preserve authoritative patchset identity; exact checkout; trusted-main classifier/normalizer/vote code; secret confinement; exclusive routing; complete `vote.needs`; fail-closed conclusions; closed-change race handling; non-voting observability; and exact markers.\n- `jira-dc-capability-map.yml` — Preserve manual amd64 authoring, pinned harness, required Anthropic access, bounded agent run, read-only repository store, teardown, and artifact.\n- `jira-dc-epic-link-probe.yml` — Preserve the manual stdlib/four-call disposable-Jira probe, no LLM or repository mutation, teardown, and artifact.\n- `jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml` — Preserve mirror-first/Gerrit-fallback exact fetch/SHA verification; mismatch/all-skip failure; DC extra; isolated no-remotes suite; teardown; additive non-Verified role; and summary/log evidence.\n- `jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml` — Preserve manual Anthropic investigation, shared harness, direct-provider overlay, read-only repository store, bounded run, evidence upload, and teardown.\n- `mirror-guard.yml` — Preserve 15-minute/manual replication checks, multiple samples, public/default-token reads, cancellation, and exclusion of admin-only ruleset drift.\n- `optionality.yml` — Preserve mirror caller filters, pull requests, manual/staggered health, read-only/no-vote posture, and branch-head reusable invocation.\n- `prompt-eval.yml` — Preserve offline branch/PR/manual evaluation; advisory same-repo changed-rubric evaluation; canonical weekly/manual live evaluation; sequential cases, cap 12, provider dollar caps, summaries/artifacts, concurrency, and exact marker.\n- `reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` — Preserve rollback input, cadence/window, single flight, write/read permissions, full-history store, optional signing, consecutive-red lifecycle, binding fsck, synchronous merge-not-rebase push, dry-run, and terminal stale red.\n\nPaths are relative to `.github/workflows/`. Consumers are GitHub Actions, repository policy tests, bridge/runtime code, and operators.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] DD `comment-only-diff` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `directive-preservation` exits 0.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and named consumer has a leaf-linked TSV row with full before/final citations.\n- [ ] Every required TSV row has a non-empty `reviewer_session`.\n- [ ] Every `reviewer_session` identifies a reviewer who did not author the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited block has one TSV row satisfying `before_words > after_words`.\n- [ ] Every edited-block row records `semantic-preservation=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every edited-block row records `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] No required TSV row is missing.\n- [ ] DD `workflow-contracts-core` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `workflow-contracts-gerrit` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `workflow-contracts-jira-dc` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `workflow-contracts-canary` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `workflow-contracts-parity` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `diff-integrity` exits 0.\n- [ ] DD `repository-gate` exits 0 without a timeout.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded deterministic commands. The independent TSV, not exact prose retention, is authoritative for concision and semantic preservation.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_artifact-probe.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_eval-discipline.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_mutation.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/codeql.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/external-integration.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":".gi